  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1048 PM CDT THU OCT 22 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery this evening reveals an upper ridge building\njust off to our west as an upper trough exits to our east. At the\nsurface, high pressure remains in control of the region. Dry\nconditions look to continue over the next week as the upper ridge\nexpands and moisture remains limited. As a result, high temps\nwill warm into the mid to upper 70s daily with lows dropping into\nthe 40s. With that said, a reinforcing surge of high pressure\nwill knock a couple of degrees off our highs over the weekend\nwith most struggling to reach the mid 70s.\n\nOtherwise, light winds and clear skies will promote patchy river\nfog overnight into the early morning hours daily over the next\nfew days.\n\n95/Castillo",
